  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 141 AM EDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\nQuiet weather through Thursday under high pressure with the next \nchance for rain coming on Friday into the weekend. A shortwave \ntrough rounds the top of the western CONUS ridge and closes off \nacross or just south of the Great Lakes. \n\nAn associated surface low meandering across the Ohio Valley \nbrings a moist easterly flow into Lower Michigan where mid level \nf-gen forcing and instability should bring rain and embedded \nthunderstorms with some diurnal enhancement on Saturday. Afternoon\nshowers could linger into Sunday and even Monday before the upper\nlow gets kicked out.",
